# Installing opm

File: opm/docs/INSTALL.oot

opm is the openOODA package manager. It is its own repo. Version is
the git tag (RFC-0006). There is no VERSION file.

## 1. The Toolchain

- `ooda` — workflow driver
- `oodac` — compiler
- `std` — standard library
- `opm` — package manager

Each is a repo. They do not share a VERSION file.

## 2. Layout

The dispatcher is `cli/main.oo`. Public surface is the 10 subdirs
counted by `scripts/verify.oo`: core, resolve, lock, store, registry,
policy, sign, launch, qa, cli.

`opm/std` is a local compile pointer to the std repo. The contract
is `OODA_STD`. Do not treat the symlink as a second std.

## 3. The Version Contract

Version is the git tag. `scripts/verify.oo` asserts `api_surface=10`
and refuses a VERSION file. See `versioning.oot`.

## 4. Run

Need `OODA_COMPILER` pointing at oodac. Need `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` to
write. Then:

```
opm <subcommand>
```

`ooda` may wrap this as `ooda opm`. That wrap is in the ooda repo.

## 5. Verify

```
oodac run scripts/verify.oo
oodac run scripts/test.oo
```

`opm` with no args prints help. Help names must match `cli/main.oo`.

## 6. Update

Pull this repo. Push to main tags the next PATCH (RFC-0006).

## 7. Tokens

| Token | Use |
|---|---|
| `OODA_COMPILER` | spawn oodac |
| `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` | write root |
| `OODA_CONFIG` | extra registry list (else `.ooda-cache/config`) |
| `OODA_GIT` | git clone for ingest |
| `OODA_CURL` | HTTPS fetch |
| `OODA_MINISIGN` | index verify / bot --sign |
| `OODA_MINISIGN_SK` | bot --sign secret |
| `OODA_UNTRUSTED` | refuse launch --exec |

Missing token is Err. No PATH hunt. No HOME.
